<section class="panel">
	<div class="hero">
		<div class="left">
			<div class="eyebrow">POCO X3 NFC &middot; postmarketOS &middot; Plasma Mobile</div>
			<h1>Linux on the POCO X3 NFC, with the hardware actually working.</h1>
			<p class="lede">Three cameras, calls, sensors, GPS, both speakers, 60 and
			120&nbsp;Hz. Flash one image and the phone works. 78 kernel patches, ten
			patched packages and six applications, in a signed repository that keeps
			itself current with <code>apk upgrade</code>.</p>
			<div class="btns">
				<a class="btn" href="install-image.html">Flash the image</a>
				<a class="btn ghost" href="devices.html">What does not work</a>
			</div>
			<div class="grid tight">
				<div><div class="num">3</div><small>cameras</small></div>
				<div><div class="num">78</div><small>kernel patches</small></div>
				<div><div class="num">68</div><small>packages</small></div>
				<div><div class="num">1</div><small>image, everything in</small></div>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="right">
			<div><b>Works</b>Cameras &middot; calls &middot; LTE &middot; sensors &middot; GPS &middot; audio &middot; 120 Hz &middot; power-off</div>
			<div><b>Does not</b>Fingerprint &middot; stereo speakers &middot; echo on calls</div>
			<div><b>Image</b>1 GB download, includes the browser, mail, maps and the six own apps</div>
			<div><b>Updates</b><code>sudo apk upgrade</code></div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section>
	<div class="wrap">
		<div class="h"><span>01</span><h2>The short way</h2></div>
		<p>Download, check, flash. The image carries everything: kernel, hardware
		fixes, the six own applications and the optional ones.</p>
		<div class="sh">
			<div class="bar"><i></i><span>ON YOUR PC</span></div>
			<pre>sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS
xz -d utsugi-surya-*.img.xz
fastboot flash userdata utsugi-surya-*.img   <b># userdata. never boot.</b>
fastboot reboot</pre>
		</div>
		<div class="note"><i></i><div>
			<b>U-Boot first, and it depends on your panel.</b>
			A phone that has never run postmarketOS needs U-Boot on <code>boot</code>
			before this. Wrong panel, black screen.
			<a href="install-pmos.html">Full first-install steps &rarr;</a>
		</div></div>
		<p><a class="btn" href="install-image.html">Download and full instructions</a></p>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="panel">
	<div class="wrap">
		<div class="h"><span>02</span><h2>Other ways in</h2></div>
		<div class="grid">
			<a href="install-image.html">
				<div class="n">Ready image</div>
				<p><b>Recommended.</b> One file, everything inside, 5 minutes. Not
				encrypted.</p></a>
			<a href="install-repo.html">
				<div class="n">Already running postmarketOS?</div>
				<p>Add the repository and one package. Keeps your data.</p></a>
			<a href="install-pmos.html">
				<div class="n">From scratch, your own install</div>
				<p>U-Boot, pmbootstrap, then the repository. For a phone that has never
				run Linux.</p></a>
			<a href="install-encrypted.html">
				<div class="n">Encrypted</div>
				<p>You build it. A LUKS key born on somebody else's machine is not
				yours.</p></a>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section>
	<div class="wrap">
		<div class="h"><span>03</span><h2>What you get</h2></div>
		<div class="scroll">
		<table>
			<tr><th>Cameras</th><td>All three: 64&nbsp;Mpx rear, front and ultra-wide,
			with autofocus. C-PHY support written for CAMSS and three sensor
			drivers.</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Calls</th><td>Voice in both directions over LTE. Echo on the other
			end is still open.</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Audio</th><td>Both speakers, earpiece, saved volume. Out of the box
			the phone booted mute.</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Sensors</th><td>Accelerometer with rotation, light, compass,
			proximity.</td></tr>
			<tr><th>GPS</th><td>Twelve satellites, fix in about 40&nbsp;s cold.
			postmarketOS ships the engine locked; this unlocks it.</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Screen</th><td>60 and 120&nbsp;Hz, with a power-saving mode that
			uses it.</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Power</th><td>Power-off that powers off, charge screen when plugged
			in while off, USB-C that can charge instead of feeding your laptop.</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Apps</th><td>Six written for this phone: navigation, screenshots,
			always-alive apps, battery per app, smart unlock, find-my-phone.
			<a href="packages.html">All of them &rarr;</a></td></tr>
		</table>
		</div>
